UNIT cmp_ver
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@b15b56613f9d cli/features.mjs cmpVer and isVersion — the spec-version comparison behind rdv's coarse gate
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG cmp_ver(a: text, b: text) -> i64
ENVELOPE any two well-formed Unicode texts (no lone surrogates). A text that is not a VERSION (PINNED below) throws (R1);
  every pair of VERSIONs yields -1, 0 or 1. Non-text arguments are out of the envelope (the js file says they throw).
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Compare two dotted version texts as sequences of non-negative integers and return the sign of a minus b:
  -1 when a is older, 0 when equal, 1 when a is newer. rdv refuses a bundle when cmp_ver(specVersion, supported) is 1.
BEHAVIOR
R1 VALIDATE — a is checked, then b: if either text is not a VERSION -> throws. The WHOLE text must match, with nothing
  before or after: no whitespace or line break at either end, no sign, prefix, suffix, exponent, empty segment, leading or
  trailing full stop, leading zero ("0" alone is the only segment that may start with 0), or non-ASCII digit. The throw
  message is not graded.
R2 SEGMENTS — a VERSION is cut at each full stop "." into segments; each segment is a non-negative integer of ANY size,
  read exactly (no rounding, no width limit: "9007199254740993" is greater than "9007199254740992").
R3 PAD — when one version has fewer segments, its missing trailing segments count as 0 ("0.5" equals "0.5.0").
R4 ORDER — walk positions from the first; at the first position whose integers differ the result is -1 if a's is smaller
  and 1 if larger; if none differs the result is 0.
R5 The result is always exactly -1, 0 or 1.
INVARIANT cmp_ver(a, b) = -cmp_ver(b, a) on versions, and cmp_ver(a, a) = 0.
PINNED grammar VERSION = SEG ( "." SEG )* CITED R1 — SEG = "0" | NZDIGIT DIGIT*; DIGIT = the ten ASCII digits, NZDIGIT = "1".."9"; the grammar covers the whole text
ORACLE value -> oracles/cmp_ver.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 fa0b26db62debb57c18b54882bb03c800470f0573183e991db0825c03d42cce4
NOTE 24 frozen + 96 held-out stamped by selfhost/stamp.mjs (seed 1) from the pinned authority: 57 curated (padding, huge segments, one probe per malformed class), then seeded fill, mostly valid.
SCOPE IN: R1–R5 over any pair of texts. OUT: semver precedence (prerelease, build metadata), a "v" prefix, a decimal
  reading of a segment ("0.10" is newer than "0.9"), and non-text arguments.
PROVENANCE rederive@b15b56613f9d (MIT), cli/features.mjs exports cmpVer + isVersion; callers cli/rdv.mts specStatus (the
  coarse gate) and cli/features.mjs specVersionFor. Cut 2026-10-26 under REDERIVE_SELF_PLAN Tier 1; round 2 re-cut after
  the round-1 findings were fixed in the kernel.
